arted competing after  transition no one really thought that i  would do well everyone pretty much just  wrote me off because they looked at me  and thought oh he's a trans guy there's  no way that he can compete against men  hearing people say that really motivated  me to work harder to learn more to be  more dedicated to my training  and try to be the strongest competitor  that i could be  even though i made team usa i was  ineligible to compete at the world level  because of the international olympic  committee policy which stated  transgender athletes needed to have a  full lower surgery performed in order to  qualify  adding an extra body part is not going  to make me a faster runner or a stronger  cyclist  they just needed an athlete with a name  and a face  someone who was actually being impacted  by this policy to look at it and to say  this isn't right the international  olympic committee changed their policy  for transgender athletes and no longer  have the same restrictions they had  before  i was so thrilled when the policy was  changed for myself but i was even  happier that the policy has now changed  for everybody who comes after me i will  not be competing in rio because duathlon  is not an olympic sport but i am so  excited to someday see a transgender  olympian compete on behalf of our  country what used to be the ceiling is  now the floor  you

